From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SwitchVN <switchvn@example.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] winedmo/wm_reader: treat a decommitted allocator as end of
 stream

Starting a video and then stopping it could make the game bail out with an
error box:

  warn:quartz:BaseMemAllocator_GetBuffer Not committed
  err:wmvcore:wm_reader_read_stream_sample Failed to allocate sample of 11889 bytes, hr 0x80040211
  trace:quartz:MediaEventSink_Notify graph, code 0x3, param1 0x80040211
  trace:win:set_window_text L"Error Abort. : [0x80040211] Error: 0x80040211"

Stopping the graph decommits the allocators, and that races against the
reader thread, which may still be pulling samples.  wm_reader_read_stream_sample()
passed VFW_E_NOT_COMMITTED straight back to its callers, which turned it into
EC_ERRORABORT and the application aborted playback.

A decommitted allocator only means the graph is going away, so report it the
way the callers already handle a stream that has run out: NS_E_NO_MORE_SAMPLES
marks the stream as EOS and everything winds down quietly.

This is the same race that could deadlock the DMO wrapper; whichever side wins
decides between the two symptoms.

Found on ATRI -My Dear Moments- (AppId 1230140).
---
 dlls/winedmo/wm_reader.c | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/winedmo/wm_reader.c b/dlls/winedmo/wm_reader.c
index 1111111111..2222222222 100644
--- a/dlls/winedmo/wm_reader.c
+++ b/dlls/winedmo/wm_reader.c
@@ -2417,9 +2417,20 @@
 
     if (FAILED(hr = wm_stream_allocate_sample(stream, capacity, sample)))
     {
-        ERR("Failed to allocate sample of %lu bytes, hr %#lx.\n", capacity, hr);
         free(stream->current_data);
         stream->current_data = NULL;
+
+        /* The allocator is decommitted while the graph is being stopped, which
+         * races with this thread still pulling samples.  That is not a failure:
+         * report it as the end of the stream so callers wind down quietly
+         * instead of raising EC_ERRORABORT at the application. */
+        if (hr == VFW_E_NOT_COMMITTED)
+        {
+            TRACE("Allocator is no longer committed, treating as end of stream.\n");
+            return NS_E_NO_MORE_SAMPLES;
+        }
+
+        ERR("Failed to allocate sample of %lu bytes, hr %#lx.\n", capacity, hr);
         return hr;
     }
 
